[{"id":"VRCE-4-24-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":1,"english":"After Rāma had spoken thus, Laksmana, the slayer of foes, addressed Sugrīva, senseless with grief, with the following sound words.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.261,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"048628b79f08d9ed057ba0db973de1ab043550d0e28508dbe0e71ac0d8332d19","compact":"6edca132414debadc6018d8cc764629957c1e38c1b5b95eca57a78067293268b","nasal":"da456cb21845ae462e12ed2a87868c62e61d54dbbd8d25615da901bad4007b27"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":2,"english":"Grief and lamentations do not tend to the welfare of the deceased. It therefore behoveth you to perform the after ceremonies.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5ad17033a62562699c66821b8ddf4ef1ab3571cfbde0cd5bc30c985569beb4a3","compact":"d6a2d38415cd457dcef354b636e541510654e5dad940ec0bfc4b66f48327fe1c","nasal":"2a07427517ed0118013a3c538e3651d28811968ab704a88ee556b06615d024d2"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":3,"english":"You have satisfied the worldly practice with a profuse discharge of tears. It is not proper to delay the performance of appointed actions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e03a95a5bd8961539beba87dbe80ba59e6ad46c5eb06a79bbaf53dcdaa9d0ffc","compact":"f35cdf7ebe961bf879ed8e0a47a45d5b0c69eb83e559336858aad35057e1650a","nasal":"f35cdf7ebe961bf879ed8e0a47a45d5b0c69eb83e559336858aad35057e1650a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":4,"english":"Time is the prime cause in this world, and the source of the accomplishment of actions. And Time it is that leads men to actions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.93,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ab3eb084065fb029360fd545f65badcc55185f5e77a478f02932a39e2fb18088","compact":"6f600cf92ca25c721cfb172a87b910d2d1b91681ba600d7932bc2a07c538e815","nasal":"6f600cf92ca25c721cfb172a87b910d2d1b91681ba600d7932bc2a07c538e815"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":5,"english":"No one is the lord of another person, and no one leads him to actions. People are subject to their actions of previous existence and Time aids them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.812,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1a1e10b6d798a2c0108ee3d234959bb3b38035c041ef66a75724106f1c07dace","compact":"eb6c58126c15aaccdbeafcd04dc734a2c0ea72c7aa047f2b704f83737c6edc49","nasal":"abae56f1796fed023386cf16564b77de5a153928ed3d8fe054a19acb53b565d2"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-6","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":6,"english":"Even the Eternal being cannot withstand the ways of Time. He never decayeth-and no one else can withstand the course of Time.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.83,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3cbf593a0c219bb2c9f9be7067dfbc41ca8ca3e9f17a87a07774b6b5d63583b8","compact":"3966ba2e8d1a1171b0e5a989056023feb57602b836e645b3b7412a13d018cb3d","nasal":"3966ba2e8d1a1171b0e5a989056023feb57602b836e645b3b7412a13d018cb3d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":7,"english":"It has no friend, no cause and no one can overcome it. It has no kinsman, no relation; even it is not subject to itself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"728ac2ae33ac1086a8799682198f3fa60d3e1a1a4f807c1e788264492c661070","compact":"0b0906cc52bd87d133b3159a834c39ee332bec3da265ebae096073aab8b221a2","nasal":"e8584ba356c41707bb2cbba9ddb7a7453b2b66007538b1e3b72d606444b3eee7"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":8,"english":"The wise can perceive the work of Time. Piety, wealth and desire are all subject to it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b4fe5cb72734fd4bb062744c984b2f7b69903701b50652fe993947693606c441","compact":"7614bab9ca044838a901e8f7ae635e146d986e7f918b9988d930fe0f147b45d7","nasal":"7614bab9ca044838a901e8f7ae635e146d986e7f918b9988d930fe0f147b45d7"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":9,"english":"Vāli, the lord of monkeys, has attained to his own true state, reaping the fruits of his actions, acquired by virtue of his royal accomplishments namely forgiveness and charity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.739,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c595ecf338f20d1e87e2cdc554282b2f946aa85a1576abb0f37b942a4c17c7f9","compact":"4282ba2f40c45af73d5695c88fff0232c72faaf1e2293b1e0b2e4e6229ed4dad","nasal":"4282ba2f40c45af73d5695c88fff0232c72faaf1e2293b1e0b2e4e6229ed4dad"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":10,"english":"The abode of the celestials, which was conquered by this high-souled one by his former piety, has now been occupied by him after resigning his body.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5e82adab49ffba3a817a88a0a8738ce742f99dd4c10f39bcc4350964b90e29e2","compact":"2436fe299db65b359533f983abe923722f1e393f67b79dbe190dda63dc7d4125","nasal":"2436fe299db65b359533f983abe923722f1e393f67b79dbe190dda63dc7d4125"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":11,"english":"This is the best course of Time that has been attained to by the lord of monkey-herds. No more with lamentations therefore; do you perform the actions that are worthy of being performed on this occasion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"88f980c93e109e74a376cc4fbb7903442a0cf7097623b265a349822867a48062","compact":"860a1fddb208dfdc7dc2f9f7319e94b98889d77ab680bf1ec8e14be16cb235df","nasal":"860a1fddb208dfdc7dc2f9f7319e94b98889d77ab680bf1ec8e14be16cb235df"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":12,"english":"After Rāma had spoken thus, Laksmana, the slayer of foes, addressed Sugrīva, senseless with grief, with the following sound words.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.983,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7ff0f7d561b947a0255f3f17370932b132ae0c891e61e152194397058780f40d","compact":"0ac7a0d4fa6fa128ceb01883ce397c43b2fd8c8bf8452c25ab7666550befdd1b","nasal":"96b62858249c2d3e3173ebe3bf0635046c49813608434c3f5963c0170259f1b4"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":13,"english":"Sugrīva, do you perform the funeral ceremonies of Vali along with Tārā and Angada.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ff2078d4419dadc0a884b359d8a304d4cfe024704ba743a6bfbf9d91fbcab383","compact":"a62826e24b7547ccc26acca49afb6e4b72746769793fb5db5cbd483f5ebd4891","nasal":"f5532691d77042dbd9ae12a676045bd43a0f9e4ba9ccdcac864686ea08d046a4"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":14,"english":"Do you collect for cremation many a dry fuel and celestial sandal.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21cdf70fc635f11433e744aea39af1df36b68ccc293ef2829447e529f7540720","compact":"dec478219b6125550e48812e03de7e7be771d6f09937b0e80eb98694c6bd4b6e","nasal":"19b3a7ec24fd31344dc433c3db19beaf803c560bf74595e98c751f496d4237be"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-15","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":15,"english":"Do you console the unfortunate Angada, who is beside himself with grief. Do not conduct yourself like an ignorant person, for this city is now under you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.726,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5855708437f7ebbdaf9791a34b8e3407c88f8feed1e1756c63d9252d9df62967","compact":"507efd7f8600b69e3a15a8f7b7cc43052769cad4ea50744d805eb0f346a89e7d","nasal":"5ce2e0f2bdc0c9b7f7754fdde523123122db0941713f89b2c629052a0a81fd71"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-16","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":16,"english":"Let Angada bring clothes, garlands, scents, clarified butter, oil and other necessary articles.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024016","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3fe2c958fd4d514a1d1a9a5dfe85a60e7180359536b19fc80b183c3df14207d3","compact":"8d6c7f9d73a2ac3efc27a9e82a731751362a43536087ed0098c00d11f9c26900","nasal":"b6ab77fbe263a2b1410b5d7b02d0729655fdc8b91dcb5d38a4e72a794377eb63"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-17","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":17,"english":"O Tārā, do you go and bring soon a conveyance; for speediness is a special virtue on an occasion like this.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024017","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2d7b0e73ef4daa847b52b0665912338b1cf979e1b63b8b2d00efc4a6b7d5e335","compact":"09effaeb0d5295538d53ba7b3bababc2ec5b41a2a671798ebe9a73ae6bbe6f11","nasal":"09effaeb0d5295538d53ba7b3bababc2ec5b41a2a671798ebe9a73ae6bbe6f11"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-18","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":18,"english":"Let the monkeys dress themselves who can convey this hearse. The powerful and the capable only shall carry Vali.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024018","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6acfc0534d079e483105c42ca77a3797a16e25b97fb30a1642f9bfb26570b28b","compact":"7609d4a137df96ccbbdbebcae636e62af6984efadd342f88bd571217b7a381e8","nasal":"8d1fdc6cca6e9c28f24e065bfa473ea18fb86ccd1218c6b14289199d3b3d580c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-19","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":19,"english":"Having thus addressed Sugriva, Laksmana, the enhancer of Sumitrā's joy and the destroyer of foes, stood before his elder brother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024019","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"803a4eaa9f3ae3bd5846a346001f6dda1022dd2798c0d4ae98ba772fe8beda85","compact":"ce03a80f174ab678a38f0e064441963e599a063f415082577e17ceb5d438fb8f","nasal":"eb4e04456657f2d7c87057b8402874ece19bf884c1041ba51a2d10edb56fd3d9"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-20","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":20,"english":"And hearing the words of Laksmana, the counsellor respectfully entered the cave with a view to bring the conveyance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024020","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c542b0c2c75ffebde86d55809a41fa1aca57a4652f1a878063714f432443930","compact":"1f289227bc7b6983d4d2c713e855c781e969e68541a5dd7edbf55d8259b842c2","nasal":"b2b1e39dcbe10ae1595f3417790e7b9ade48cb5d15e42cb639f8c918b94a58db"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-21","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":21,"english":"And taking that conveyance carried by the monkeys and worthy of being carried by the heroes, he issued out again of the cave.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.729,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024021","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bd91f08a08f51a31bea70f1491ac36f32649cc48e1ae7f3857409278e6756bd7","compact":"5fa570ff3ed45483c25eab6affa8053a3fa83ac957ac895c68a8b1de4dd8bf62","nasal":"5fa570ff3ed45483c25eab6affa8053a3fa83ac957ac895c68a8b1de4dd8bf62"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-22","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":22,"english":"Thereupon Sugrīva, long with Angada, placing Väli on the conveyance, began to bewail.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024022","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c2174f6b841dc8a828f670ee5a720187ee816ef7c82449f0bbd1c2394dcdb77e","compact":"4c94719deee112350472e45c6c45d23df04756a20b3bcfa8c7443479d948e36a","nasal":"c3f582a8b9bcfbd0e22c06eccc63007039a26ca9ec6a54a139aeb7154bfb8107"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-23","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":23,"english":"And placing the lifeless body of Vāli on it, he covered it with various ornaments, garlands, and clothes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.94,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024023","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ba6f4bbb39cce28dd1d398a78f5d232f59a72539ce31d3465e4391aef5828bcd","compact":"b73e9e77fec0a099c175fb8d223d0966119b78a52be14bde624155f9fc4367ee","nasal":"b73e9e77fec0a099c175f