ewailed on all sides.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.776,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024029","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aef6496b371676816595ff21a840f6c6672bcb5ad32afb15935b590760b45da4","compact":"173bec8bad47a5ac5d96d4bc53459d8ed46181c54e217c73c4d07caa97d8ef48","nasal":"aedfb362271994a3d5584801f62dae5e9683c243f62c3a3bfde6b1f2a3ff82f3"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-30","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":30,"english":"Monkeys, ranging in the forest, made funeral piles on the banks of the hill-streams and in solitary watery nooks. Thereupon laying down from their shoulders the conveyance, those foremost of monkeys stationed themselves in a corner, being stricken with grief.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024030","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7fa33aca145c7458f74c0c71ab254aceb7af518960ad55789beb8ee8e76dfd5e","compact":"57b655fccd5ed5ca41dde975e50b4d5f4c3e34b1ce0e4b8c6163ecd7caffef06","nasal":"57b655fccd5ed5ca41dde975e50b4d5f4c3e34b1ce0e4b8c6163ecd7caffef06"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-31","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":31,"english":"Monkeys, ranging in the forest, made funeral piles on the banks of the hill-streams and in solitary watery nooks. Thereupon laying down from their shoulders the conveyance, those foremost of monkeys stationed themselves in a corner, being stricken with grief. And Tārā, beholding her husband's body on the conveyance, placed his head on her lap and bewailed, overwhelmed with griet.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.333,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-35","DUTT-4-25-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024031","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c17058caa1ad89953685cf5a477269d797d1112c9c1fd2b3cc4f09ce4a78cdaa","compact":"465050c9c294c2e16938f223f0e1fe607adcbd91636cfcf47f87495caafdb792","nasal":"463b770796b1d15c0702e10b961b69363484422feb8c3a17569d0c9ed39fa901"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-32","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":32,"english":"And Tārā, beholding her husband's body on the conveyance, placed his head on her lap and bewailed, overwhelmed with griet.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024032","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8c335b77335034c519c2516f4f4c0c3d1b1c5d2f1af1fa277214f641001fefb6","compact":"91ef472b7bc927b51a3d63bd451836707530ce20b7f1683a78accd495b4ddc5a","nasal":"430a69a6068d295e42f01bd7dbda49b90e305dd2d4bbab295d2f92e42acb4f1b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-33","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":33,"english":"O lord of monkeys! O my lord! O my dear one! O you used to luxuries! Oyou having long arms! O my darling! behold me. Why did you not behold these monkeys, racked with sorrow? O conferrer of honours, your countenance looks as if beaming with joy; although you are dead, and you appearest as if alive, having the hue of the setting Sun.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.409,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-37","DUTT-4-25-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024033","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"13095883d77e80885367aface85d283efb4419875b0a1c482506ee96b9888732","compact":"67ae93e8b7ebf9d7d35b16440297e5fad3efa6eae0b4ded35b11e4e53c2b86ec","nasal":"ae2ff0a57db433010ebdb4a354529e659a1019f752fa6ae46c0f06a9b8c2635b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-34","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":34,"english":"O monkey, Death himself, under the semblance of Rāma, is attracting you, who with one shaft in the battle, has rendered us all widows.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024034","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21aedc91047d06055cd9f6531070b7c104311ef6ddf68bbd9b546bcc24eccacf","compact":"d5f09cab7acbadec687268e0edc6664496f15aaf942b0b46cd491d3224e79aa3","nasal":"d5f09cab7acbadec687268e0edc6664496f15aaf942b0b46cd491d3224e79aa3"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-35","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":35,"english":"O best of kings, these she-monkeys cannot go by jumping. Did you not perceive that they have travelled so far on foot?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024035","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7521ee72d32d5b2aa1456db26555760ec2d0d67063c462db616bc93cf75fb9ca","compact":"aad491617a409ff96065962a4275d4ee203a8d109225c87fe8c54ba70f6682de","nasal":"ea588f7bd28b065b652046887110cfda35bbd8c96ac969d8af14b4c4f1d15a66"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-24-36","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":24,"verse":36,"english":"Those your wives, having moon-like countenances, have always your welfare in view. Why did you not, O best of monkeys, cast your looks towards them and Sugrīva?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.69,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-25-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4024036","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"05f34b424748788725b6e2074203ee0be2eb13e246fc63d0ce7087a2839fdb54","compact":"9be0337aa7bc6a0afcd84bf2e85a177d0dcc66a36d9f9929e6ee51d